Z||000000||Jncomutt||04-08-2001||11:52 AM||||I just bought a 84 2m4 for the interior is perfect and only has 50000 miles.  Problem with the car is that as soon as the engine cranks over, the check engine light is immediatly on.  The idle jumps from just about to stall (and sometimes does) up to just over 2000 RPMs.  When I checked for a code, its reading only a Code 22.  What does this mean, What should I check first, and How can I fix it???  Any help or suggestions at all would be greatly appreciated.   Thank You <P>Sorry About the Mix-up...  It reports a Code 22.   NOT Code 44.  Dunno what I was thinking<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 04-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||RacinRob||04-08-2001||04:56 PM||||Check out this site, no it's not for the fiero but the codes are the same, at least 22 is it will give you the info<BR> <A HREF="http://www.syty.org/d&e.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.syty.org/d&e.html</A> <P>it is low voltage TPS Throttle position sensor<BR>||||reg||1
